  "id": "etf_rev",
  "family": "reversal",
  "title": "Among sector and industry funds, buy the week's laggards against the leaders",
  "why": "Sector funds trade for a basis point or two, so a reversal too small to survive a stock's spread could survive here. Flows into and out of sector funds push them away from the market for days at a time and then relax. Against it: at one month, sectors show momentum (Moskowitz and Grinblatt 1999), so the week may simply be noise.",
